cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata in this file.
  Please also cite the sources of the method, listed under references.
title: RandomizedTukeyHSD.jl
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-11
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: White
    given-names: Jerome
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4148-8834"
repository-code: "https://github.com/jerome-white/RandomizedTukeyHSD.jl"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A Julia implementation of the randomized Tukey HSD test for comparing many
  treatments over a shared set of blocks. In each trial the responses are
  shuffled across treatments within every block, and the largest minus the
  smallest treatment mean is recorded. A pair's p-value is the fraction of
  trials whose range is at least the pair's observed difference. The package
  also reports the Monte Carlo error of the p-values and chooses the number
  of trials from a precision target.
keywords:
  - randomized Tukey HSD
  - randomization test
  - multiple comparisons
  - Monte Carlo
  - Julia
